---
import { DISPLAY } from '@tonalisk-labs/kit/theme';

import site from '../../../marcoferra.config.json' with { type: 'json' };
import { TEXT_LINK } from '../booking/classes.ts';
import { durationOf, eventTypes, methodsOf, paidTypes, priceOf } from '../booking/event-types.ts';
import Section from '../components/section.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/layout.astro';
import { EMAIL } from '../lib/json-ld.ts';

const ADDRESS = 'Av. Dom João II, 52, Piso 0, 1990-096 Lisboa, Portugal';
const {
  hold_minutes: holdMinutes,
  refund_until_hours: refundHours,
  withdrawal_days: withdrawalDays,
} = site.booking;
const [firstPaid] = paidTypes();
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of use, marcoferra.com"
  description="The terms that apply when you book a free or paid session on marcoferra.com: prices, payment, cancellation, refunds and your right of withdrawal."
  image="terms"
>
  <article class="flex flex-col gap-6">
    <h1 class={DISPLAY}>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="text-slate-700">Last updated 8 October 2026.</p>

    <Section id="provider" title="Who provides the service">
      <p>
        Marco Ferra, {ADDRESS}, reachable at
        <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`} class={TEXT_LINK}>{EMAIL}</a>. These terms apply to every
        session booked on this site.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section id="service" title="The booking service">
      <p>
        You can book a video call with Marco Ferra at a free time on this site. A free session is
        booked once its invitation has been sent to your email address. A paid session is booked
        once its payment is confirmed. The invitation then follows by email. Every invitation
        carries the Google Meet link and a link to cancel. Sessions cannot be moved: to change the
        time, cancel and book another, under the cancellation terms below.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section id="prices" title="Sessions and prices">
      <ul class="flex list-disc flex-col gap-2 ps-5">
        {
          eventTypes().map((kind) => (
            <li>
              <strong>{kind.title}</strong>: {durationOf(kind)}, {priceOf(kind)}.
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <p>
        Prices are final. No VAT is charged: IVA, regime de isenção, art. 53.º do CIVA. An
        invoice-receipt (fatura-recibo) is issued for every paid session, and Stripe emails its own
        payment receipt.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section id="payment" title="Payment">
      <p>
        A paid session is paid in advance on Stripe's secure checkout page{
          firstPaid === undefined ? '' : `, by ${methodsOf(firstPaid)}`
        }. The time you chose is held for {holdMinutes} minutes while you pay. If the payment is not
        completed, the hold ends and nothing is charged. Card and account details are entered on
        Stripe's page only and never reach this site. If a payment arrives after its time was
        released or taken, it is refunded in full.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section id="cancellation" title="Cancellation and refunds">
      <p>
        You can cancel any session from the link in its invitation. A paid session is refunded in
        full, automatically and to the way you paid, when you cancel it before it starts and either
        within {withdrawalDays} days of booking it or at least {refundHours} hours before it
        starts. A paid session cancelled later than both, or missed, is not refunded. The
        cancellation page says which applies before you confirm. If Marco Ferra has to cancel a
        session, you are told by email and refunded in full.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section id="withdrawal" title="Your right of withdrawal">
      <p>
        If you book as a consumer, you may withdraw from the contract within {withdrawalDays} days
        of booking without giving a reason, as long as the session has not taken place: cancel it
        from the link in its invitation, or write to
        <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`} class={TEXT_LINK}>{EMAIL}</a>. The payment is then refunded in
        full, to the way you paid.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you book a paid session that takes place within those {withdrawalDays} days, you
        expressly ask for it to be provided during the withdrawal period, and you acknowledge that
        you lose the right of withdrawal once the session has been given in full (Directive
        2011/83/EU, art. 16(m), and Decreto-Lei n.º 24/2014, art. 17.º). The booking form asks you to
        confirm this, and the confirmation email records it.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section id="use" title="Fair use">
      <p>
        Give your own name and an address you can read. Do not book on someone else's behalf
        without their consent, send unsolicited messages, or try to exhaust the service. A booking
        made in bad faith may be cancelled, and repeated requests are limited.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section id="liability" title="Liability">
      <p>
        Sessions are advice given in good faith. Decisions taken after them remain yours. To the
        extent the law allows, Marco Ferra is not liable for indirect loss arising from the service.
        Nothing in these terms limits the rights consumer law gives you.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section id="others" title="Services it relies on">
      <p>
        The site is hosted on GitHub Pages behind AWS CloudFront, bookings run on AWS Lambda, are
        kept in Google Calendar with a Google Meet link, payments are taken by Stripe, and emails
        are sent through Maileroo. The
        <a href="/privacy/" class={TEXT_LINK}>privacy policy</a> says what each of them handles.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section id="complaints" title="Complaints and disputes">
      <p>
        Write first to <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`} class={TEXT_LINK}>{EMAIL}</a>. You may also
        complain in the
        <a href="https://www.livroreclamacoes.pt/" class={TEXT_LINK}>Livro de Reclamações Eletrónico</a
        >. A consumer dispute may be taken to a Portuguese consumer arbitration centre, such as the
        Centro de Arbitragem de Conflitos de Consumo de Lisboa. The full list of alternative
        dispute resolution bodies is kept by the Direção-Geral do Consumidor at
        <a href="https://www.consumidor.gov.pt/" class={TEXT_LINK}>consumidor.gov.pt</a>.
      </p>
    </Section>

    <Section id="law" title="Law">
      <p>
        These terms are governed by Portuguese law, without prejudice to the consumer protection
        your own country gives you.
      </p>
    </Section>
  </article>
</Layout>
